  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 254 PM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nBehind the high pressure departure Thursday night, winds return to \nout of the south to southwest in the low to mid levels. This will \nlead to another surge of moisture raising dew points again and \npushing temperatures slightly warmer and conditions more humid again \nfor Friday. Winds will also be on the increase as the pressure \ngradient tightens creating breezy conditions on Friday with the \nhighest winds/gusts in northern to northwest Iowa where gusts may \nreach up to around 35 mph. \n\nTheta-e advection then ramps up late Friday night into Saturday \nmorning as the mid-level trough deepens and a surface low moves \nthrough the region dragging a cold front with it. This will bring \nour next chance for showers and storms, mainly overnight Friday \nnight into early Saturday morning. SPC maintained the day 3 (Friday) \nMarginal to Slight (Level 1 to 2 out of 5) in northwest Iowa for \nthese storm chances as they reach the area late into early Saturday \nmorning. \n\nThe weekend then looks to remain active with several additional \nchances for showers and storms from later Saturday into Sunday, and \nthen again with more widespread chances Sunday through Monday. \nAlthough temperatures remain in the 70s to 80s through the weekend \n(though with the higher dew points), we'll get one more bigger push \nof heat into Monday before cooling back into the 70s early next week \nbehind another cold front. Will continue to evaluate the potential \nfor severe storms and heavy rain with these subsequent rounds over \nthe coming days but conditions at first glance to remain more \nfavorable for heavy rain with pwats over 1.5\" through much of the \nweekend.",
